title: 'sp-io: Stop passing state version to storage root host functions'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    This starts ignoring the `state_version` passed to the storage root functions. This basically implements [this old rfc](https://github.com/w3f/PPPs/pull/6), but instead of deprecating the functions it changes the way the host/node is handling this. This is a preparation for [parachain service](https://github.com/paritytech/parachain-service/issues/52). Parachains on JAM will require new host functions and to not introduce the requirement there to pass `state_version` this pull requests removes the requirement.

    A later pull request will then introduce the new host functions for JAM.
